For every pull request, check whether the diff is E2E-relevant before reviewing
implementation details.

Treat changes under `backend/**`, `frontend/src/app/**`, `kong/kong.yml`,
`compose.yml`, `compose.e2e.yml`, or `mock-provider/**` as E2E-relevant unless
they are docs, Dockerfiles, lockfiles, or Go unit tests as defined in
`frontend/e2e/coverage-map.yml`.

For each E2E-relevant diff:

1. Read `frontend/e2e/coverage-map.yml`.
2. Identify the feature id whose `paths` and optional `api_routes` cover the
   changed behaviour.
3. State the existing Playwright spec that covers the behaviour, or explicitly
   flag the coverage gap.
4. When flagging a gap, recommend a concrete spec name, feature id, and scenario
   for the author or `@e2e-test-author` to add.

Review comments are advisory. Do not author the test directly during Copilot code
review; recommend invoking `@e2e-test-author` or running the `write-e2e-test`
skill when coverage is missing.
